WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
Alexander Rybak, welcome!

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:03.460
How nice!

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.100
Hello!

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:12.280
When you look back at these images,

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.240
we can see that you've already had quite a long career

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.800
since your breakthrough in 2009.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.220
And a very European career.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.860
You've been big in many countries.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.980
And now you're leaving Europe!

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.800
I would say I'm more Norway based.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.940
Even though I'm now going to Chicago.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.120
Because you are going to Chicago?

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.800
Yes I am. Okay. I am going to Chicago.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.860
What's the deal, you're going to attend school?

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.420
Oh, Fredrik, this is a new chapter in my life! It's so much fun!

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.660
It's great fun! I'm doing a master's degree

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:51.780
in ... It's said to be among the top three film music schools in the world.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.520
So I'm very privileged.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.820
It's so much fun and I already feel like I've been given a new family.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:03.060
And it's online, and then my mum will appear in the background with shrimp sandwiches!

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:07.040
They see love first and foremost, but I'm a bit embarrassed.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.200
But up until now, no one's mentioned it.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.660
You've moved within many genres, you've worked in many countries,

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:19.760
you've done an incredible amount of things since your breakthrough.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:24.260
As I mentioned initially, this came at a price.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.120
And with that I mean

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:33.660
a post that you shared in social media earlier this summer.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.980
Which to a lot of people was very surprising, including to me.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.500
And it was about to what degree you've been a pill addict.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.900
And eaten too many medicines.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.460
It started with

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.960
something that was supposed to help me with sleep. I'm a

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:55.020
highly sensitive person.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.560
For instance, I considered earlier to try to act laid-back,

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.040
you look so cool when you ...

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.940
But that's not me, I'm always highly alert.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:10.300
And when you're participating in the world's biggest music competition,

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.880
and you're as sensitive as me,

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:14.940
you end up having extreme difficulties falling asleep.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.840
And sleep is very important when you're going to

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:23.040
use your voice, play the violin and in general function as a human being.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.120
So now we're in 2009 and your breakthrough with Fairytale?

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.200
Yes.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.600
So I got a little help with sleeping pills,

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.920
very innocent and a very small dose.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:41.340
And all of a sudden, all these constant nuisances disappeared, where nothing was good enough,

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.740
that I would stop myself when speaking,

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:48.020
that I forgot to breathe, everything just disappeared

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.200
the last 30 minutes before I fell asleep.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.440
And I thought, «ah, this is life»!

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:58.680
And then it just became more and more the following years.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.820
When did you realise that you

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:04.660
had a form of addiction?

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.680
I never understood it. I never understood it.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:13.100
I understood that this was something that I wanted to keep doing on a daily basis.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:13.980
Preferably.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:18.200
But I didn't think about abuse or addiction, I didn't think in those terms.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:22.040
I just thought that I had found the pill that made me whole.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:27.900
But there are a lot of people who take a sleeping pill once in a while and who

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.300
are just fine with that. But for you, that has

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:35.180
had a big impact, maybe also on you personality?

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.380
Yes, yes, yes. Without a doubt.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.420
It's ...

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.900
My doctors warned me all the time.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:48.400
The problem was that I had several doctors in several different countries and I

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.000
self-medicated.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.120
I was completely sure of that fact that I needed this.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.800
So when I didn't get any more from one doctor, I would ask the other.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.260
It's not good.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:59.480
What did it do with your personality?

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:03.500
When I think about it, everything

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.160
that people have heard about from the media,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:11.520
where I've thrown the bow to the ground at an event on Liseberg,

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:12.960
where I've

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.740
yelled at a sound guy,

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:22.320
where I broke my hand in a wall after a sound guy ...

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.860
The incidents were not related, by the way.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:26.840
So ...

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.980
I think that all this has happened in the evening.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.580
When the last remaining part of the sleeping pill

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.240
from the day before has disappeared.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.140
Before you've taken more?

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:40.620
Yes. The last two or three hours when your body is saying that «it's really about time».

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:47.620
And I've also noticed that with people who for instance have lived with me.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.640
When I come home at eight in the evening,

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:53.480
there was just one thing that I sub-consciously was thinking about.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.600
And that was to take your sleeping pill?

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:56.420
Yes.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.180
What kind of boyfriend did you become?

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.280
I wrote a lot of nice songs.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.220
But again ...

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:11.700
A healthy girl would most likely want to talk to her boyfriend.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:14.480
No matter how late is is in the evening.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:19.020
But I would come home from some concert at ten, and

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:24.400
it was very nice seeing her, but I would rather just watch a movie and ...

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.720
Because I knew how irritated I was as a person.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.320
Have you been

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.040
open about this?

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.800
For example when it comes to your girlfriend,

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.300
did she realise

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:41.000
that you were doing this?

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.120
Or have you been hiding it a little?

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:46.820
The problem is that I haven't been open about this with myself.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.140
That's been the biggest problem.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:51.100
It was only last year that I realised this.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.380
What about your parents, how did they react?

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:55.440
Well, everybody tried, but ...

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.780
It's like with most other things, that ...

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:02.260
There's nobody but yourself who can initiate such a difficult process

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:05.640
as getting rid of something that

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:08.280
you think is going to save you.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:11.040
You decided, as far as I've understood,

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:13.600
to wean off this,

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.020
and you made a plan.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:17.880
What did the plan look like?

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:27.100
It's to do with what I talked about, that you're in denial about what the root of the problem is.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:31.500
So when it really began to escalate and I started to get a lot of

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.700
problems with my stomach and things like that,

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.140
after a while I couldn't walk,

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:37.540
daytime I started to walk like this,

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.360
which also led to back problems.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:43.180
And it would be like «isn't that Alexander walking on the street like that?».

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:45.260
It was a little too early for that.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:47.540
And I began to understand that this ...

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:50.400
I had to get to the bottom of this.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.080
And I had

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:56.720
the premiere for my musical, last year.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:01.660
And that's the biggest thing you can accomplish as a composer, to get your own musical.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:04.340
With a million-kroner budget.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:06.720
And it was a fantastic concert venue.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:09.500
And I had to get well.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:14.500
But I refused to realise that I perhaps should quit some medications.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:18.780
I started touring around Europe to different doctors

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:23.420
and do gastroscopies and alternative doctors and lots of different things.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:26.840
I spent way too much money on it.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.240
And became completely obsessed.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:33.140
And again, the most obvious thing I didn't realise until the end of last year.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:38.200
And by then it was too late, I couldn't begin to both step down and

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:41.480
do a great part in my musical.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.000
So then I did something completely different.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.600
I began taking valium.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:48.340
Which to me worked like sleeping pills.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:52.920
And I said to myself that I would just roll with it, and in January,

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:55.260
I'll say no to every single job,

00:07:55.740 --> 00:08:00.520
and I'll only be focusing on gradually weaning off.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:03.100
And then just quit everything.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.720
And that's the worst thing I've experienced.

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:09.400
But at the same time it was the best, because I was following a plan.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:12.160
Weaning off something ...

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:15.200
what did that feel like for your body, in a physical sense?

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:18.760
I hallucinated a lot.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.580
In January, February ...

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.820
I had insane cramps,

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:28.020
I slept, at best, two hours at night.

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.200
And there were nightmares all the way.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:34.080
And my mother has some «funny» film clips where

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:38.620
I ask her to remove the ants that are crawling on my teeth.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:41.800
«No Alexander, there are no ants.» 
«Yes, come on mum, please!»

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:43.760
You thought you had ants on your teeth?

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:44.640
Yes.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.240
Alexander, you mention your family.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:57.740
You were born in Belarus.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.540
How strong is the connection between

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.680
you guys who live in Oslo

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.720
and your family who live there,

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:13.120
because you still have family there, don't you?

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:14.740
Yes, yes, yes.

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:19.960
With it being so dramatic there, what kind of contact do you have?

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:25.380
That hasn't changed, because

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.780
I've always had a good relationship with my family down there.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:33.680
And you should see my dad, it's very heart-warming ... I live with my dad and mum now ...

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:39.320
So every morning I can hear him playing accordion and piano on Skype, for his mother.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:42.060
And sometimes I'll join.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:43.220
It's very nice.

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:46.780
And they don't talk very much about politics and things like that.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:50.980
And I've been encouraged, of course, to

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:55.740
say something out loud.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:01.200
But it's easy to suddenly make the mistake of talking about something you don't know much about.

00:10:01.540 --> 00:10:03.440
I feel that

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:07.440
as a known person

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:10.840
you should really familiarise yourself with a case,

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:15.440
if you're really, really good, you familiarise yourself with a case,

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:21.300
and you should voice your opinion, especially if it's useful.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:25.400
Or, if you feel like you don't have time, you have to wait

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:29.120
until you've familiarised yourself with the case, before you talk about something you don't know anything about.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:35.020
You maybe got burned a little as well, because I can remember that many years ago,

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:38.480
there was an image of you and Lukashenko, I think, the president ...

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:43.460
I wouldn't say that I got burned. At the time he had organised a concert, and

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:49.780
it would have been strange to say that I would come but that I wouldn't agree to a picture with the organiser.

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:51.680
So it's ...

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:55.540
I haven't gotten burned.

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:56.980
No, but you got told off quite a bit?

00:10:56.980 --> 00:11:02.380
Yes, yes. But if I get burned every time I get told off, I'll become steaming hot in the end!

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:04.260
How did you experience him?

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:08.040
Shall we move on, perhaps?

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:09.840
You don't remember?

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:11.000
Yes, yes, yes.

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:14.780
But it's just that ... Even though this is

00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:16.780
a show in Scandinavia,

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:19.640
it gets watched in

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:22.500
it's watched very closely in Eastern Europe as well.

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:26.940
And that's why I want to, again, as I've said,

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:30.500
wait until I've really familiarised myself with the case before I ...

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:34.540
When I see a police offiser

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:37.980
beat up a protestant in Minsk,

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:43.400
maybe it's just me that's built in a strange way, but

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.260
I don't immediately think politics, I think

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:50.480
«he shouldn't be allowed to be a police officer».

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.700
But when you don't

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:55.520
pick a side, in a way,

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.480
are you afraid of not being able to

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:00.280
travel there again?

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:02.400
I do have family there. Yes.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:07.000
I think that they intentionally also maybe don't tell us about ...

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.660
They want to ...

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:13.820
I think that my grandmothers are very aware that I'm an artist.

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:17.300
And that the more I know, the more exposed I am.

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:20.060
Yes.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:26.240
Alexander, it's a great pleasure having you with us again.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:30.480
And we're getting in a few more guests, but you'll be with me here in Oslo.

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:32.560
Thank you! I look forward to it!

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.900
We're getting in more guests, and in the end, you'll be playing for us.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.540
Alexander Rybak, ladies and gentlemen!

